  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nA doubly degenerate shared node with constant-weight-five labels first admits the historical orthonormal-residual interface at **nine coordinates**. The proof excludes h<8 using PR920's floor and excludes h=8 by a complement isometry to the triple class in PR1139. An explicit h9 witness provides all four orthonormal residual bases, with dimensions **3,3,4,4**.\n\n**Status: structural research note; no new kappa or paid supplier.** Only research/five-subset-shared-node-seed48/ is added. Global label coverage, simultaneous frames, source access, helpers, copies/restoration, recursive pricing, hosting and analytic/precision obligations remain open.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nSeed48 (fresh OS draw), structural decoder track. Exact base: ce7ad1b6ab09452c3478723a2e96ed5ff212dc08. Scope key: five-subset / doubly-degenerate / signed-rank-one / disjoint-spans / h8-h9 / orthonormal-residuals. CLAIM.json records three candidate tasks, the local claim, complete domain and stopping rule.\n\nNearest predecessor: @woklerx's #1139, pinned at 82da1e827c51d94691134c6aec346357d89622bc, proves the triple-only ten-coordinate classification. This changes the label alphabet and adds a sharp weight-five threshold and exact census. It does not lower PR920's unrestricted norm-one h8 floor. PR920 (@ArnavSwiggy), historical head 913817423bbfaf241dec1d6b9edb1c7ded349508, supplies the residual criterion and four-plus-four bound. No pending implementation is imported.\n\nOpen PR metadata refreshed through #1171, with no matching five-subset package. CONTRIBUTING/autoresearch guidance changed during the sprint; the new discussion board was checked before submission (only its three starter threads, no overlapping claims). The explicit seed48 assignment and fixed base are retained.\n\n## Validation\n\nPython3.9.6, standard library, offline:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/five-subset-shared-node-seed48/verify.py\npython3 -I -B research/five-subset-shared-node-seed48/independent.py\n```\n\nBoth pass normally and with -O. The independent labeled set census agrees on **0 rectangles at h8 and 453,600 at h9**. The canonical frame enumeration tests all **59,520** dimension-four candidates; every canonical rectangle has exactly **48** legal frames. Both implementations independently check the witness residual spans and Gram entries.\n\nSix mathematical controls, all 65,536 h8 isometry vector pairs, all 3,136 complement-kernel pairs, optimized relocation, six malformed-certificate rejection exits, source pins, selected-record guard and staged whitespace check pass. Final read-only review caught and verified the fix for a missing-basis cardinality check. The written threshold proof and finite census are distinct evidence.\n\nNo repository-wide or selected cold supplier replay was run for this isolated historical geometry package. No hosted CI success or formal multiplication theorem proof is claimed. Selected frontier and upstream/ remain unchanged.\n\n## Credit\n\nCredit Douglas Colkitt's historical parity kernel/obstruction, @ArnavSwiggy's #920, @woklerx's #1139 and the seed47 frame-completion note. Exact sources are pinned in SOURCES.json. Prepared for **@ToikY** with substantial **OpenAI Codex** assistance in mathematics, implementation, independent algorithms and review. Apache-2.0. No independent human peer review claimed.",
